  "messages": "Maya Chen: quick design check \u2014 the clipboard icon in the Query modal is getting missed by users in testing. feels like low affordance when there's no label :eyes:\\nDevon Patel: saw that in usability too. on small screens it's just an icon with almost no hit area. suggests increasing target + add aria-label/title\\nAnika Gomez: accessibility note: must be keyboard-focusable and announce what it copies. 'Copy query' vs 'Copy to clipboard' wording matters for screen readers\\nRaj Singh: +1 for larger hit area. can we also fallback to text on narrow breakpoints? e.g., show icon+\"Copy\" when width < 480px so it's discoverable\\nMaya Chen: microcopy question \u2014 prefer 'Copy SQL', 'Copy query', or 'Copy to clipboard'? testers thought 'Copy SQL' was too technical for some product users\\nDevon Patel: leaning 'Copy query' \u2014 generic and maps to our product language. implementation sketch:\\n```\\n<button class=\\\"copy-btn\\\" aria-label=\\\"Copy query\\\" title=\\\"Copy query\\\" data-clipboard-text=\\\"...\\\">\\n  <span class=\\\"visually-hidden\\\">Copy query</span>\\n  <svg aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\">...</svg>\\n</button>\\n```\\nAdds visible tooltip on hover, and a visually-hidden label for SRs\\nAnika Gomez: that works. also add role=\\\"button\\\"? if it's a <button> element we don't need role, but ensure key handlers for Space/Enter if using div fallback\\nRaj Singh: for touch, increase padding to 12-16px and expand hit target with pseudo element so it doesn't overlap modal close btn. also let's ensure the focus ring meets contrast \u2014 current ring is very pale\\nMaya Chen: copy feedback for toast after copy \u2014 testers confused when nothing changed. propose: persistent inline confirmation near field: small 'Copied' chip that fades after 2s, plus screen reader announcement \"Query copied to clipboard\"\\ndesign-bot: accessibility audit note: \\\"Element with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" should be updated after copy to announce: 'Query copied to clipboard.'\\\"\\nDevon Patel: code for toast aria:\\n```\\n<div aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" class=\\\"sr-only\\\" id=\\\"copy-announcer\\\"></div>\\n// on copy: document.getElementById('copy-announcer').textContent = 'Query copied to clipboard.'\\n```\\nAlso will add 44x44 minimum tap target and adjust z-index so it doesn't get clipped\\nAnika Gomez: quick a11y nit \u2014 avoid using only color for the copied state. add check icon and text. contrast for the check background should be >= 3:1 against text\\nMaya Chen: design iteration: I'll mock 3 variants \u2014 (A) icon only with bigger hit area + tooltip, (B) icon+label on narrow screens, (C) icon+chip confirmation. I'll post frames in #design in 30m for quick thumbs up\\nRaj Singh: if you need a dev review I can slot 30m after standup tomorrow to look at CSS impact on modal layout\\nMaya Chen: thanks \u2014 tagging @Devon for accessibility/implementation follow-up and @Anika for a11y signoff. :thumbsup:\\nDevon Patel: cool. will prototype the aria-live approach and keyboard behavior in a small PR. will link here when ready\\nMaya Chen: perfect \u2014 leaving this thread open until PR + mock are in. small wins on microcopy + hit targets will likely bump success in next round of usability tests :)",
